sycl: fuse a short conv with its residual add and scale

HomeBrain patch on ggml-sycl. Applies on top of 0011.
Upstream tracking: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/32757

convolve() ends with SSM_CONV, a RESHAPE to [channels, tokens], an ADD of the
input stream and a SCALE by 1/sqrt(n_conv + 1). 176 of the 192 convs per decode
token are not dynamic and take exactly this chain. The conv kernel now applies
(res + conv) * scale + shift at its store and writes the SCALE node directly. That
is one launch instead of three, and the conv output is never written out and read
back. The SiLU and bias epilogue the kernels already carried moves into the same
struct. The fusion declines when the SCALE buffer overlaps the conv's input or
weights, which other work-groups may still be reading.

